WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:03.370
(audience cheers)
(audience applauds)

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:07.210
- Mr. President, Dr. Biden,

00:00:07.210 --> 00:00:11.580
Madame Vice President, Mr. Emhoff,

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:14.653
Americans and the world,

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:18.060
when day comes we ask ourselves,

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:23.060
where can we find light in
this never ending shade?

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:24.910
The loss we carry,

00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:26.540
a sea we must wade.

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:29.720
We braved the belly of the beast

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:33.690
We've learned that
quiet isn't always peace

00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:37.750
and the norms and notions of what just is

00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:40.163
isn't always justice.

00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:44.130
And yet the dawn is ours

00:00:44.130 --> 00:00:45.770
before we knew it.

00:00:45.770 --> 00:00:47.210
Somehow we do it,

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:50.740
somehow we weathered and witnessed

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:54.040
a nation that isn't broken,

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:56.230
but simply unfinished.

00:00:56.230 --> 00:01:00.000
We the successors of a country and a time

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.090
where a skinny black girl

00:01:02.090 --> 00:01:06.060
descended from slaves and
raised by a single mother

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:09.220
can dream of becoming president.

00:01:09.220 --> 00:01:12.563
Only to find herself reciting for one.

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:16.570
And yes we are far from polished,

00:01:16.570 --> 00:01:17.890
far from pristine,

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:18.870
but that doesn't mean

00:01:18.870 --> 00:01:23.210
we are striving to form
a union that is perfect.

00:01:23.210 --> 00:01:28.210
We are striving to forge
our union with purpose.

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:32.720
To compose a country
committed to all cultures,

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:37.140
colors, characters and conditions of man.

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:41.230
And so we lift our gaze not
to what stands between us,

00:01:41.230 --> 00:01:44.000
but what stands before us.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:48.110
We close the divide because we
know to put our future first

00:01:48.110 --> 00:01:50.720
we must first put our differences aside.

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:52.590
We lay down our arms

00:01:52.590 --> 00:01:55.550
so we can reach out our
arms to one another.

00:01:55.550 --> 00:01:58.950
We seek harm to none and harmony for all.

00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:03.950
Let the globe, if nothing
else, say this is true.

00:02:05.270 --> 00:02:07.960
That even as we grieved, we grew.

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:10.090
That even as we hurt, we hoped.

00:02:10.090 --> 00:02:12.440
That even as we tired, we tried.

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:15.860
That we'll forever be
tied together, victorious.

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:20.260
Not because we will
never again know defeat,

00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:25.260
but because we will
never again sow division.

00:02:25.590 --> 00:02:27.350
Scripture tells us to envision

00:02:27.350 --> 00:02:31.770
that everyone shall sit under
their own vine and fig tree

00:02:31.770 --> 00:02:34.870
and no one shall make them afraid.

00:02:34.870 --> 00:02:37.220
If we're to live up to our own time

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:39.610
then victory won't lie in the blade

00:02:39.610 --> 00:02:42.210
but in all the bridges we've made.

00:02:42.210 --> 00:02:44.480
That is the promise to glade,

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:47.430
the hill we climb if only we dare it.

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:52.430
Because being American is
more than a pride we inherit,

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:57.630
it's the past we step
into and how we repair it.

00:02:57.630 --> 00:03:00.770
We've seen a force that
would shatter our nation

00:03:00.770 --> 00:03:02.400
rather than share it,

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:07.220
would destroy our country if
it meant delaying democracy.

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:10.750
And this effort very nearly succeeded.

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:14.880
But while democracy can
be periodically delayed,

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:18.800
it can never be permanently defeated.

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:19.990
In this truth,

00:03:19.990 --> 00:03:21.580
in this faith we trust.

00:03:21.580 --> 00:03:23.900
For while we have our eyes on the future,

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:26.980
history has its eyes on us.

00:03:26.980 --> 00:03:30.040
This is the era of just redemption

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:32.200
we feared at its inception.

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:34.710
We did not feel prepared to be the heirs

00:03:34.710 --> 00:03:36.740
of such a terrifying hour

00:03:36.740 --> 00:03:40.910
but within it we found the
power to author a new chapter.

00:03:40.910 --> 00:03:43.560
To offer hope and laughter to ourselves.

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:47.130
So while we once we asked,

00:03:47.130 --> 00:03:51.620
how could we possibly
prevail over catastrophe?

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:54.530
Now we assert,

00:03:54.530 --> 00:03:59.450
how could catastrophe
possibly prevail over us?

00:03:59.450 --> 00:04:01.890
We will not march back to what was

00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:03.830
but move to what shall be.

00:04:03.830 --> 00:04:06.280
A country that is bruised but whole,

00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:09.930
benevolent but bold, fierce and free.

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:11.870
We will not be turned around

00:04:11.870 --> 00:04:14.350
or interrupted by intimidation

00:04:14.350 --> 00:04:18.010
because we know our inaction and inertia

00:04:18.010 --> 00:04:20.790
will be the inheritance
of the next generation.

00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:23.450
Our blunders become their burdens.

00:04:23.450 --> 00:04:25.533
But one thing is certain.

00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:29.710
If we merge mercy with might,

00:04:29.710 --> 00:04:31.830
and might with right,

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:35.380
then love becomes our legacy

00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:39.320
and change, our children's birthright.

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:41.660
So let us leave behind a country

00:04:41.660 --> 00:04:43.850
better than the one we were left with.

00:04:43.850 --> 00:04:46.370
Every breath from my bronze pounded chest,

00:04:46.370 --> 00:04:50.090
we will raise this wounded
world into a wondrous one.

00:04:50.090 --> 00:04:53.420
We will rise from the
gold-limbed hills of the West,

00:04:53.420 --> 00:04:55.860
we will rise from the windswept Northeast

00:04:55.860 --> 00:04:58.630
where our forefathers
first realized revolution.

00:04:58.630 --> 00:05:01.000
We will rise from the lake-rimmed cities

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:02.660
of the Midwestern states,

00:05:02.660 --> 00:05:04.630
we will rise from the sunbaked South.

00:05:04.630 --> 00:05:08.060
We will rebuild, reconcile and recover

00:05:08.060 --> 00:05:10.310
and every known nook of our nation

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:12.690
and every corner called our country,

00:05:12.690 --> 00:05:16.010
our people diverse and
beautiful will emerge

00:05:16.010 --> 00:05:17.330
battered and beautiful.

00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:20.520
When day comes we step out of the shade,

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:22.390
aflame and unafraid,

00:05:22.390 --> 00:05:25.570
the new dawn blooms as we free it.

00:05:25.570 --> 00:05:27.450
For there is always light,

00:05:27.450 --> 00:05:30.140
if only we're brave enough to see it.

00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:34.093
If only we're brave enough to be it.

00:05:36.336 --> 00:05:38.202
- [Man] Woo!
(audience applauds)

00:05:38.202 --> 00:05:41.702
(audience cheers lightly)

